  "final_message": "The bug is fixed and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` passes.\n\nThe problem was that `add_tag` defaulted `tags` to a shared list (`tags=[]`), so tags from one call leaked into the next. It now defaults to `tags=None` and creates a new empty list inside the function when `tags` is omitted. When a caller passes their own list, `add_tag` still appends to that same list, which I checked separately. `remove_tag` is unchanged.\n\nDONE: Fixed the mutable default in add_tag so calls without tags get a new empty list and a passed-in list is used as given; public test passes.",
