      "final_message": "I rewrote `solution.py` so `semver_compare(a, b)` follows the README, and both tests in `test_public.py` pass.\n\n- **Wrong type:** anything that isn't a string raises `TypeError`.\n- **Invalid format:** a string is rejected with `ValueError` unless it is exactly `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`. That means ASCII digits only, no leading zeros, and no pre-release tags, build metadata, spaces or trailing newline.\n- **Comparison:** it compares `(major, minor, patch)` as tuples of numbers and returns `-1`, `0` or `1`, so `1.10.0` is newer than `1.9.9`.\n\nI also ran some extra checks of my own for these edge cases, and they passed.\n\nDONE: Rewrote semver_compare to validate strict MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH strings (TypeError for non-strings, ValueError for anything else invalid) and compare them as number tuples; public tests pass.",
